{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310745,"nonce":"+FlPEUWPCKJnibXhxEWKwgaCFEs=","title":"WASM backend zeroes all fields of an anonymous struct (typedef object literal) when returned from a function — current top-of-stack blocker ...","message":"**Fact:** On the wasm32 backend, an anonymous-struct value built via an\nobject literal and returned from a static function arrives at the\ncaller with every field zeroed/empty. Reproduced 2026-06-08 in\n`GGUFLoader.metadataFromReader`:\n\n```haxe\nprivate static function metadataFromReader(reader:GGUFReader):ModelMetadata {\n    var arch = reader.metaString(\"general.architecture\");\n    // trace inside: arch = 'llama' (correct)\n    ...\n    return {\n        architecture: arch,         // 'llama'\n        hiddenSize: hiddenSize,\n        maxSeqLen: maxSeqLen,       // 2048\n        ...\n    };\n}\n\n// caller:\nvar meta = metadataFromReader(reader);\n// meta.architecture = '' (empty)\n// meta.maxSeqLen     = 0  (was 2048)\n```\n\nBoth a `String` field and an `Int` field arrived empty/zero, so this\nis not a String-specific marshalling bug — the whole struct is being\nconstructed wrong on return. Native MIR path is fine.\n\n**Why:** Probable bug in `wasm_backend` for `ReturnValue` of a freshly\nallocated anonymous-struct. Hypothesis: the callee allocates a fresh\nobject pointer for the return value, but the field-init writes go to a\nDIFFERENT (stale) pointer — possibly a register the SROA / phi-lowering\npass forgot to update at the function epilogue. Or the caller reads the\nstruct at a stale address. Not root-caused yet.\n\nThe fact that `[lwt] 4 → 5 → 6` all pass (meta is alive enough that\ndownstream `weights.isQuantised` works) suggests the struct itself is\nallocated and reachable — only its fields are zeroed.\n\n**How to apply:** When wasm-side code returns an anonymous-struct\n(typedef object literal) and the caller sees empty fields:\n1. Suspect this bug before looking at the field assignment site.\n2. Workaround: convert the typedef to a real `class` with a constructor\n   that stores the fields, or pass an out-parameter that the callee\n   mutates.\n3. The wasm load path through `GGUFLoader.loadWithTokenizer` will hit\n   this in `metadataFromReader` and again in `LoadedModel { model,\n   tokenizer, metadata }` (the load function's own return), so the\n   fix needs to cover both call sites.\n\n**Fix path:** Inspect `wasm_backend.rs` lowering for `ReturnValue` of\nstruct-typed values. Cross-check with the native MIR path that works.\nThe fix should ensure the return-value's struct pointer is consistent\nbetween the field-init writes and the caller's reads. Add an e2e\nregression: a typedef object returned from a function, all primitive\nfield types covered (String, Int, Float, Bool).\n\n**Status:** Top-of-stack blocker as of 2026-06-08 commit 34d74c8. With\nthe bytes-in-linear-memory arc landed\n([[perf_wasm_bytes_in_linear_memory_arc]]), all 147 GGUF tensors load\ncleanly; the next trap is `ArchRegistry.build` failing because\n`metadata.architecture == ''` so no builder is found.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_wasm_anon_struct_return_zeroed` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}